ve thousand pounds  worth of data online which is then sold  to marketing companies and harvested  filtered and cross-referenced to provide  detailed insights into our lives  facebook will know you're gay long  before your mother does  seventy percent of us admit to fearing  how much we've already shared one in  seven teenagers in the us has sent a  compromising image over the internet and  had a sexual chat with a real life  stranger a majority of european internet  users are under the impression that a  security service has snooped into their  conversations and activities  4. online crime is out of control  over the last 20 years crime has abated  in many countries since it peaked in the  uk in 1995 it's fallen by 60 percent but  internet crime is exploding in 1990 the  nspcc estimated there were 7 000 known  images of child pornography at large  in 2014 american law enforcement found  42 million images on just one server  the uk government estimates that 50 000  people in the uk are actively involved  in downloading and sharing images of  child abuse online abuse and hate speech  are endemic on twitter 10 000 uses of  racist slur terms occur a day and 2 000  tweets are sent containing the word rape  69 of young people in the uk have  experienced cyber bullying the police  are overwhelmed the head of the uk's  national crime agency recently said that  they would only ever be able to focus on  less than one percent of all child porn  users  conclusion  one view is that new technologies have  always brought anxieties with them and  that they always turn out to be  groundless socrates in plato's phedris  warned that books would promote  forgetfulness people would become the  hearers of many things and will have  learned nothing  but that's too rosy and too relaxed  about what we're facing technologies can  and do bring serious lasting problems as  the residents of hiroshima realized the  internet presents unrivaled challenges  to our abilities to interact deeply with  our partners keep our critical faculties  alive stop thinking that the answers  always lie out there remain emotionally  connected to real life people and make  the discoveries that come when we're  bored and let our minds lie fallow we  need to start to take active measures to  educate our children in the dangers of  this tool to reconnect with the natural  world to talk to one another face to  face to stop downloading images of naked  people to get bored and to take regular  digital sabbaths we need to learn to  control ourselves not because the  internet is so bad but precisely because  it's so very very nice in ways that turn  out to be deeply detrimental to our  ability to flourish and to function  we can accept that it's not a good thing  to let a 15 year old boy have  unmonitored access to the internet in  his bedroom not because we think he's  wicked but because we're generous we  understand that asking for self-control  in those circumstances is too demanding  a similar argument applies if you happen  to be 26 or 46 the internet has an  unparalleled power to get in the way of  almost every other important and  precious thing around starting with the  rest of your life  you
 

